  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Monday)\nIssued at 1132 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nA cutoff low over the southeastern US has finally shifted far\nenough east as to have lost its influence on the Mid-South.  As a\nresult, warmer temperatures and clear skies have returned to the\nregion.\n\nA ridge will shift over the Southern Plains today, shunting the\ntrough east. As the ridge builds in from the west, temperatures\nwill trend closer to normal today. Expect highs in the middle 80s\nto lower 90s. Heat indices should remain below 100 degrees.\n\nTomorrow, the ridge will deamplify and transition across the\nMississippi River Valley, initiating a warming trend with low to\nmid-90s expected from Thursday through the weekend. This pattern\nwill suppress convection through Thursday, with only marginal\nrain chances (20-30%) returning by Friday.\n\nThe weekend into early next looks hot and humid, but nothing\nunseasonably warm. Increased cloud cover Friday through the\nweekend may keep temperatures in check a bit, but increasing\nhumidity will boost Heat Indices nonetheless. Heat index values\nHeat Advisory criteria of 105F should be mostly confined to the\nMS Delta region, south of Memphis.  There is uncertainty into how\nbroad or deep the trough will emerge, which will heavily\ninfluence temperatures and precipitation this weekend. For now, a\n20-40% PoP was maintained through the weekend.",
